P(egg is bad) = \frac{\text{number of bad eggs}}{\text{total number of eggs}}
= \frac{4}{30}
= \frac{2}{15} or 0.133 or 13.3%

P(egg is good) = \frac{\text{number of good eggs}}{\text{total number of eggs}}

= \frac{26}{30}

= \frac{13}{15} or 0.867 or 86.7%

Or, P(egg is good) = 1 - P(egg is bad)

= 1 - \frac{4}{30}

= \frac{26}{30}

= \frac{13}{15} or 0.867 or 86.7%

